      "name": "What is Anthropic Contextual Retrieval?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Contextual Retrieval is a technique pioneered by Anthropic that solves context loss in RAG. Before embedding, an LLM generates a 50–100 word succinct situational summary explaining where the chunk sits within the broader document. This context header is prepended to the raw chunk before generating vector embeddings and BM25 lexicons."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does Anthropic Prompt Caching reduce chunk enrichment costs?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "By placing the full original document (e.g. 50,000 tokens) into Claude's prompt cache, subsequent chunk enrichment calls reuse the cached prefix. Anthropic discounts cached input tokens by 90%, reducing chunk enrichment costs from ~$1.50 per 100 pages down to ~$0.15."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does Contextual Retrieval improve RAG retrieval accuracy?",
